WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.705
Mastery Starter 1.0.

00:00:02.705 --> 00:00:04.925
New to Foundations & Safety?

00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:05.985
Start here.

00:00:05.985 --> 00:00:08.072
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:08.072 --> 00:00:09.765
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:11.065 --> 00:00:14.987
Most crypto losses aren't market losses; they're mistakes and

00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:17.834
scams: a seed phrase typed into a fake site,

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:21.550
an approval signed without reading, the wrong network.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.305
This module builds the habits that prevent them.

00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:28.844
Private key: the secret that signs transactions.

00:00:28.844 --> 00:00:31.819
Approval: permission for an app to move a token.

00:00:31.819 --> 00:00:35.364
Multisig: a wallet that needs several keys to act.

00:00:35.364 --> 00:00:38.259
Phishing: a fake site or message built to steal.

00:00:38.259 --> 00:00:41.639
Simulation: a preview of what a transaction will change.

00:00:42.939 --> 00:00:47.654
First, Module 0 done (secured exchange, restore-tested wallet).

00:00:47.654 --> 00:00:49.430
And finally, A small amount in

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.149
a wallet on a low-fee network.

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:54.993
Open your wallet's approvals (or a revoke

00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:57.840
tool), list every approval you've granted, and

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.354
revoke any you don't use.

00:01:00.654 --> 00:01:02.613
Beginner: Uses a separate burner

00:01:02.613 --> 00:01:04.694
wallet and reads every prompt.

00:01:04.694 --> 00:01:08.174
Practitioner: Runs the before-signing checklist without

00:01:08.174 --> 00:01:11.084
notes; limited approvals; hardware wallet.

00:01:11.084 --> 00:01:14.159
Master: Multisig vault, simulation on every

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:17.374
signature, private addresses, tested recovery.

00:01:18.674 --> 00:01:21.534
You've mastered this module when you can take

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.524
a new app from first visit to a

00:01:23.524 --> 00:01:27.379
limited, simulated, verified transaction, and revoke it after.

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:31.194
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:31.194 --> 00:01:33.587
Next up, Lesson 1.1: What DeFi

00:01:33.587 --> 00:01:35.979
is, and the risk-first mindset.
